Who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven? (Mark 9:33-37; Luke 9:46-48)
At that time the disciples came to Jesus and asked, "Who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?"
And Jesus called for a little child and set him in their midst.
He said to them, "Truly I tell you, unless you change and become like little children, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven."
Whoever makes himself humble like this child is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven.
How can someone accept me just because I have my name?
But if it should be an obstacle to someone who believes in God, then let him have a millstone hung around his neck and thrown into the sea.
Oh my God, what things make people commit sins? Those things have to come, but oh my God, the person who brings those things that lead people to sin!
If your hand or leg is causing you to sin, cut it off and throw it away. It's better for you to enter eternal life with one limb missing than to have both hands and feet intact but end up in hell forever.
If your eye causes you to sin, pluck it out and throw it away; it is better for you to lose one part of your body than for your whole body to be thrown into hell. It is easier for heaven and earth to pass away than for one dot of the law to become void.
Be careful, don't underestimate someone who has kids. I tell you, their angels in heaven are always looking at God's face up there.
There are ancient texts that say this verse: "I am the Son of Man who came to save those who were lost."
What do you think? If someone has 100 sheep and one gets lost, wouldn't he leave the 99 in the mountains and go look for the lost one?
Tell me the truth, if you can find it, he'll be happier with it than ninety-nine who didn't lose anything.
"But if your brother sins against you seven times in a day, and turns to you seven times, saying, 'I repent,' you must forgive him." - Luke 17:3
If your brother wrongs you, go to him in private and point out his mistake. If he listens to you, then you've won over your brother.
But if he doesn't listen to you, take one or two more witnesses with you so that every word spoken has at least two or three witnesses testifying about it.
If he won't listen to them, tell the church; if he won't listen to the church either, treat him like an unbeliever or a tax collector.
I'll tell you the truth: whatever you tie up here on earth will be tied in heaven, and whatever you loosen here on earth will be loosened in heaven.
I'll tell you again: if two of you agree about anything you ask for here on earth, your Father in heaven will do it for you.
Where two or three gather in my name, I am there among them." Like an unmerciful servant
Then Peter came to Jesus and asked, "Lord, how many times shall I forgive my brother when he sins against me? Up to seven times?"
Jesus said to him, "I do not say to you seven times, but seventy-seven times."
That's why the kingdom of heaven is like a king who wanted to settle accounts with his servants.
When he started to settle his accounts, they brought him someone who was asking for money without keeping track.
As he couldn't pay off his debt, Sayed Pasha was forced to sell himself, his wife, children, and everything he owned in order to settle his debts.
My friend, the servant fell to his knees and said: "Oh my master! Please be patient with me and I'll get everything done for you!"
He was mocked by Seydou and Seibou, and they forgave him for his debt.
But this servant went outside and found another one like him asking for some money. The guy got angry and said to him: "Just give me the money you're asking for!"
My friend, another servant fell off his camel and begged me to be patient until we finish our business.
He didn't love her and left. They put him in jail until he pays off his debt.
The other servants found out what happened, got really worried, left, and went to tell their master about the mess that was made.
At that time Nadalou said to him: "O wicked slave! I have forgiven you this debt because of your good service."
And you don't have the right to spare your servant friend just like I spared you?
And Tughashh Sido, and they handed over to the responsible person for detention until he pays off his debt in full.
"This is how your heavenly Father will also treat each one of you if you don't forgive your brother from your heart."
Marriage and Divorce (Mark 10:1-12)
Jesus continued speaking. He left Galilee and went to Judea across the Jordan River.
Many people followed him, and he healed them all.
Some Pharisees came to test him. They asked, "Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife for any reason?"
Tell them: "Bro, haven't you read that He who created them in the beginning created them male and female?"
Mk 1:27; 2:24; Mt 5:31; Mk 6:16 And he said to them, "This is why a man leaves his father and mother and clings to his wife, and the two become one flesh?"
"But they're no longer two; they have become one body. That is why God says 'What God has joined together, let man not separate.'"
The Pharisees said to him, "Why then did Moses command us to give a certificate of divorce and send her away?"
Jesus said to them, "Moses permitted you to divorce your wives because your hearts were hard. But it wasn't like that in the beginning."
And I'll tell you this: anyone who divorces his wife for anything other than adultery and marries another woman is committing adultery himself.
The disciples said to him, "If this is how it is between husband and wife, then it's better for them not to get married."
But he said to them, "Not everyone can accept this teaching; it requires special people."
