He left with nine others, man. He saw some other guys standing in the market looking for work
He said to them: "Go pick some grapes from that vineyard, and I'll give you what is rightfully yours. But they didn't go."
He went out again about noon, then at three in the afternoon, and did the same thing.
He came out about five o'clock in the evening and found some other people sitting there; he asked them what they were doing there all day long.
They said to him: "Even if one person asks us for help we'll serve them." He told them: "Then you too go work in the vineyard."
As evening approached, the vineyard owner said to his servant who was busy with other tasks: "Go call all the workers and pay them their wages, starting from those hired last until you reach me."
And so the group who started serving with the five loaves took their place, each one receiving a silver coin.
And when they came to the governor, each one thought he would get more than the others; but in fact, each one received two talents of silver.
And while they're finishing up, you can cheat with the grapes
