He answered one of them: "My friend, I haven't wronged you. Didn't we agree to sell silver?"
Take what's yours and leave. I wanted to give them this just like I gave it to you.
Bro, don't I have the right to do whatever I want with my money? Or are you jealous because I'm generous?"
Jesus said, "The Son of Man is going to be betrayed into human hands." Jesus told them for the third time about his death and resurrection (Mark 10:32-34; Luke 18:31-34)
As Jesus was going up to Jerusalem, he took the twelve disciples aside and said to them along the way:
